## Task board

This project's work is tracked on a local Agent Board, not in your own memory. The project name on the board is `PROJECT_NAME`.

Report your progress by calling the `agent-board` CLI directly via your shell/bash tool:

```bash
agent-board list --project=PROJECT_NAME
agent-board create --title="..." --project=PROJECT_NAME --agent=claude --priority=med
agent-board update <id> --status=in_progress --agent=claude
agent-board note <id> "short note about what happened" --agent=claude
```

Always pass `--agent=claude` explicitly — don't omit it even though the flag is technically optional; leaving it off means the board can't tell who left a note or made a change.

**When to call it:**
- At the start of a coding task: `list` first for an existing open ticket matching the work; if none exists, `create` one and set it `in_progress`.
- Whenever status meaningfully changes (code is ready for review, you're blocked, you're done).
- When you hit a blocker or make a non-obvious decision: `note` it.

**Important:** always call `list` fresh when you need the board's current state — never assume it still matches what you saw earlier in the conversation. Someone else (a person, or another agent) may have changed it since.
